From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0423-t33-ocarina-amd-fixes.patch

Source: 0423-t33-ocarina-amd-fixes.patch
Moved by hand: the fragment_writes_color member added beside fragment_has_color0_output (the writes_storage line it expected is not in this tree)

each behind a switch

All off by default. Each one is a port, kept as close to the source as the tree allows.

EDEN_NX2_BLEND_ALWAYS=1, mja00/Lichii f00aa63884 (from sharkiix): blend state is rebuilt at every
refresh. Native Switch 2 paths write blend registers without raising Dirty::Blending, which leaves
a stale state on a device without dynamic blend. The PS5 logs dynamic state level 2, so it takes
this path.

EDEN_NX2_PLAIN_SAMPLER=1, mja00/Lichii 05a9fb2dca (from sharkiix): a plain sample through a
compare-enabled sampler uses a variant without comparison.

EDEN_NX2_MASK_UNWRITTEN=1, mja00/Lichii c52c24239f: colour targets the fragment shader never writes
are masked.

EDEN_NX2_QUERY_WAIT_ONCE=1, mja00/Lichii cbf4f704c8: one wait per occlusion query resolve. The
source limits this to AMD's own drivers; here the switch decides, since RADV also waits per query.

EDEN_NX2_WFI_BARRIER=1, Lichii 18cfe85563 (PR 295): wait for idle is a pipeline barrier. The event
it used is never reset, so only the first wait of a session waited.

Not run yet.
